<title>THAILAND: BOXING-CHATCHAI WINS VACANT WBC FLYWEIGHT TITLE.</title>
<headline>BOXING-CHATCHAI WINS VACANT WBC FLYWEIGHT TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Chatchai Sasakul won the vacant World Boxing Council flyweight crown on Friday with a unanimous decision over first-ranked contender Isaias Zamudio of the United States.</p>
<p>The WBC stripped Russia's Yuri Arbachakov of the title because he did not defend it in time due to a wrist injury.</p>
</text>
